  {
    "formula": "f(x)=0 \" for \" x<1, quad f(1)=1",
    "text": "This is pointwise convergence: each fixed input gets its own eventual control. But the limit jumps at one. The increasingly steep graphs near that endpoint show why controlling each location separately is not the same as controlling every location simultaneously.",
