  {
    "formula": "g_n(x)=frac(x,n), quad sup abs(g_n(x))=frac(1,n)",
    "text": "Compare x divided by n on the same interval. The error from zero is at most one over n for every input at once. A single index therefore works across the whole interval, establishing uniform convergence.",
